<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n45377" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔυδρ-ος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕδωρ</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>well-watered, abounding in water</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄστυ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Simon.
					96
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκτά</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>P.</u>
					1.79
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Μαραθών</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Call.
					<u>Hec.</u>
					1.1.8
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νάπη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Nic.
					<u>Al.</u>
					622
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γῆ ποιώδης καὶ εὔ</span>.
				<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				4.47
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χῶρος -ότερος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					9.25
				</span></i>
			; [
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄρη] -ότερα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Gp.</u>
					2.6.5
				</span></i>
			 (
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν</span>
			-). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> of a river or
			spring, <i>with beautiful water</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κάσας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					B.
					10.119
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Εὐρώτας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>IT</u>
					399
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κασταλίς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Pae.Delph.</u>
					5
				</span></i>
			; so prob. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔυδρον ποτόν</span>
			(vulg. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔνυδρον τόπον</span>) <i><span class="en">
				Polyzel.
				2
			</span></i>.</div>
